      "id": "2ae40848-715c-4b8a-bc4c-11c7f492a11a",
      "name": "Prepare Post Data"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "return $input.all().map(item => {\n  const likes = Number(item.json.likes || 0);\n  const comments = Number(item.json.comments || 0);\n  const shares = Number(item.json.shares || 0);\n  const postText = item.json.post_text || \"\";\n\n  return {\n    json: {\n      post_text: postText,\n      posted_at: item.json.posted_at,\n      likes: likes,\n      comments: comments,\n      shares: shares,\n      total_engagement: likes + comments + shares,\n      post_length: postText.length\n    }\n  };\n});"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        944,
        64
      ],
      "id": "12cb3785-93bf-4e7d-918c-470845648787",
      "name": "Calculate Engagement Metrics"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Analyze the LinkedIn engagement data provided below.\n\nFor each LinkedIn post:\n\n1. Summarize the post.\n2. Report its likes, comments, and shares.\n3. Calculate total visible interactions as:\n   likes + comments + shares\n4. Compare the posts using the available engagement data.\n5. Identify noticeable content patterns.\n6. Give practical recommendations for future LinkedIn posts.\n\nImportant:\n\n* Use only the data provided.\n* Do not invent impressions, reach, engagement rate, or other missing metrics.\n* If a metric is not provided, say that it is unavailable.\n* These posts may be very recent, so avoid making strong conclusions from very small engagement numbers.\n\nReturn the analysis using these sections:\n\nOverall Summary\n\nPost-by-Post Analysis\n\nEngagement Patterns\n\nRecommendations\n\nHere is the actual LinkedIn data:\n{{ JSON.stringify($input.all().map(item => item.json)) }}\n",
        "options": {}
      },
